    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d256-a2">

                <pb facs="0449" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg415"/>

                <head>Mr. Lushington to Mr.
                        Hammond.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiralty,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 9, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>S<hi rendition="#small-caps">ir</hi>: In reply to your letter of this day
                    requesting that copies of the recent instructions given to Vice-Admiral
                    Wellesley for the protection of the Canadian fisheries may <pb facs="0450"
                        n="416" xml:id="pg416"/> be sent to you for communication to the Government
                    of the United States, I am commanded by my lords commissioners of the admiralty
                    to transmit to you a copy of a letter addressed to the vice-admiral on the 9th
                    of April, (of which you were informed by letter of the same date,) and of a
                    letter addressed to him on the 5th instant, on a representation from the
                    secretary of state for the colonies.</p>
                <p>My lords request that you will lay the same before the Earl of Clarendon.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>VERNON LUSHINGTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
